This patch implemented the falsified "placeholder-forward verification
commit" hypothesis (FINDINGS.md Addendum 2). The real corruption was later
root-caused to stale gathered-block-table reads and is fixed by 0009+0010.
Worse, this gate silently rejects every draft for any request rescheduled
within pp_size sample-steps of its last — at concurrency 1 that is EVERY
step, capping MTP decode at ~1 token/step (~2.5x throughput loss) while the
pre-gate acceptance metric still reads normally (Addendum 18).
Kept only as a historical record of the investigation.

Subject: [Spec][PP] Never commit MTP verification decisions computed from
 placeholder-input forwards

Status: PROTOTYPE / RFC — design validated by measurement, code not yet
verified end-to-end (see repro below). Applies on top of PR #46994.

Under async pipeline-parallel scheduling, a request can be rescheduled
before its previous outputs have propagated to the first rank. Rank 0 then
embeds placeholder (zero-init) tokens for the sampled/draft positions.
That is by design for plain decode: need_sampled bookkeeping ensures those
forwards' samples are never used, and the state is rolled back.

With MTP, however, rejection sampling on the last rank runs on the logits
of that same placeholder-poisoned forward and its accept/reject decisions
ARE committed. Accepted garbage converges on the drafter's unconditioned
argmax, producing constant-token degenerate loops (~14-27% of requests
whenever max_num_seqs >= 3; measured threshold exactly 2->3 slots, flat
above, absent without PP or without MTP).

Fix direction: extend the per-request need_sampled mask into the
verification path. For any scheduled request whose inputs this step were
built from unpropagated state (equivalently: need_sampled == False for
the positions being verified), force num_accepted = 0 and exclude its
bonus token from commitment, exactly mirroring how plain decode discards
placeholder-forward samples.

--- a/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py
@@ (in sample_tokens, after rejection sampling produces num_sampled/num_rejected)
+        # PP + spec decode: verification decisions from placeholder-input
+        # forwards must not be committed (mirrors need_sampled handling for
+        # plain decode). Placeholder steps are those where the request was
+        # rescheduled before its prior outputs propagated (< pp_size steps).
+        if self.pp_handler is not None and self.speculative_config is not None:
+            stale = compute_placeholder_mask(input_batch, self.req_states)
+            if stale is not None and stale.any():
+                num_rejected[stale] += num_sampled[stale] - 1
+                num_sampled[stale] = 1  # keep only the (rolled-back) bonus slot
